# Accepted exceptions for the development image (dockle).
# Production runs on Clever Cloud, this image is only used locally and in CI.
# Any new finding not listed here must be fixed, not appended in a hurry.

# sudo is installed on purpose: devs need it from `make ssh`, which logs them in
# as the unprivileged `dev` user.
DKL-DI-0001

# Direct consequence of the line above (sudo is a setuid root binary).
# suexec, the other setuid binary shipped by apache2, has been removed instead.
CIS-DI-0008

# The image ends as root because Apache must bind port 80 then drop privileges,
# and the php-fpm master must be able to spawn its workers.
# Devs work as non-root through `make ssh` (--user=dev).
CIS-DI-0001

# Development image, rebuilt constantly and referenced by name in
# docker-compose.yml, the Makefile and the CI. This rule targets deployed images.
DKL-DI-0006

# DOCKER_CONTENT_TRUST would break the build: the third-party images in use
# (surnet/alpine-wkhtmltopdf, composer/composer) are not signed through DCT.
# Integrity is covered differently: the Surnet image is pinned by digest.
CIS-DI-0005
